    "body": "Crescat Capital founder and CEO Kevin Smith.\nPosted By: Henry Lazenby October 9, 2026\nWeakening participation in the Nasdaq rally signals a possible market top, says Crescat Capital founder and CEO Kevin Smith, whose firm hedges some funds against a selloff that could also hit junior miners.\nAlongside that defensive positioning, Crescat is backing explorers, with Smith naming BCM Resources (TSXV: B), Sitka Gold (TSXV: SIG) and Eloro Resources (TSX: ELO) as its three largest holdings. Their principal projects are Thompson Knolls in Utah, RC Gold in Yukon and Iska Iska in Bolivia, respectively.\n“And we found that the best way to invest in the segment is through a diversified portfolio,” he told The Northern Miner’s Western Editor, Henry Lazenby, last month at the Precious Metals Summit in Beaver Creek, Colo.\nThe firm manages $600 million (C$855.9 million), with more than 70 companies in its activist metals portfolio, Smith said. Its strategy centres on financing drilling to establish and expand discoveries. He expects further results to enlarge Sitka’s gold resource, while acknowledging that exploration remains a risky investment.\nWatch the full interview below:\nPrint\nTAG: Video\nCOMMODITY: base metals Gold Silver\nREGION: United States\nCOMPANY: BCM Resources Crescat Capital Eloro Resources Sitka Gold\nRepublish this article",
